From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] DVDInputStreamBluray: a 3D disc is played as a 3D player
 plays it

Kodi tells a disc it is a profile 6 player - an Ultra HD Blu-ray player
- and Ultra HD Blu-ray has no 3D. The Java program of a 3D disc reads
the profile and the display's 3D capability before it shows its first
screen, and finding a player that cannot play its 3D it took a path
that never comes back: the disc stood on its first still for good, its
language or warning screen answered a key and then went black.

A disc with 3D content is now told the player is profile 5, the 3D
profile, and that the display shows 1080p and 720p 3D - true of Kodi
on any display, since it shows 3D as the display takes it, and some
discs' programs wait for a 3D display as they wait for the profile.
Every other disc is told what it was told before.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStreamBluray.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStreamBluray.cpp
index 988ba14..7ea9b7a 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStreamBluray.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStreamBluray.cpp
@@ -356,6 +356,17 @@ bool CDVDInputStreamBluray::Open()
   else
     CLog::Log(LOGERROR, "CDVDInputStreamBluray::Open - BluRay not detected");
 
+#if (BLURAY_VERSION >= BLURAY_VERSION_CODE(1, 0, 2))
+  // A 3D disc's Java application looks for the 3D profile, which a UHD player is not, and for a
+  // display that shows 3D - which Kodi gives it on any display, as the display takes it: without
+  // them it waits for good on its first screen.
+  if (disc_info->bluray_detected && disc_info->content_exist_3D)
+  {
+    bd_set_player_setting(m_bd, BLURAY_PLAYER_SETTING_PLAYER_PROFILE, BLURAY_PLAYER_PROFILE_5_v2_4);
+    bd_set_player_setting(m_bd, BLURAY_PLAYER_SETTING_DISPLAY_CAP, BLURAY_DCAP_1080p_720p_3D);
+  }
+#endif
+
   if (disc_info->aacs_detected && !disc_info->aacs_handled)
   {
     CLog::Log(LOGERROR, "CDVDInputStreamBluray::Open - Media stream scrambled/encrypted with AACS");
